Thank you for providing some information. Let's proceed with creating your personal webpage using the details you provided. Below is a single-file HTML code for your webpage:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Abhish's Personal Webpage</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      margin: 20px;
    }
    h1 {
      color: #007BFF;
    }
    p {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    a {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #007BFF;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Welcome to Abhish's Personal Webpage</h1>
  <p>Hi there! I'm Abhish, and this is my personal webpage. Here are a few things about me:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Name:</strong> Abhish</li>
    <li><strong>Hobbies/Interests:</strong> sdfsd, sdfdsfaa</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you'd like to get in touch or learn more about me, feel free to connect through one of the following:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email: <a href="mailto:your.email@example.com">your.email@example.com</a></li>
    <li>LinkedIn: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/yourusername">linkedin.com/in/yourusername</a></li>
    <li>GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/yourusername">github.com/yourusername</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Thank you for visiting my webpage!</p>
</body>
</html>
```

Please replace `your.email@example.com`, `yourusername`, `sdfsd`, and `sdfdsfaa` with your actual email address, your LinkedIn profile URL, your GitHub profile URL, and your hobbies or interests respectively. 

Copy and paste this entire code into a text editor and save it with the extension `.html`. Once you have done that, you can open the file with a web browser to see your personalized webpage. Remember to upload this HTML file to a web server if you want it to be accessible publicly.
